BE002 --> BE004[\"B-E004 Dashboard connection UI\"]\n        BE002 --> BE005[\"B-E005 docs\"]\n        BE003 --> BE005\n        BE004 --> BE005\n    end\n\n    E001 --> AE002\n    E001 --> AE003\n    E001 --> AE004\n    E001 --> AE005\n    E001 --> AE006\n    E001 --> AE007\n    E001 --> AE008\n    E001 --> BE002\n    E001 --> BE003\n    E001 --> BE004\n    E001 --> BE005\n```\n\nNote: there is deliberately **no** edge between A-E004 (konflux-onboarding)\nand A-E005 (Platform Operator implementation) — they run in parallel; the\nimage-digest coupling is enforced by an acceptance criterion on A-E005, not a\nDAG dependency.\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → every branch epic | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | The posture decision determines whether each branch epic exists at all. True gate: `remove` — every branch epic carries `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-9007-E001` and a `gate_failure_impact` of `remove`. Two bounded outcomes → conditional decomposition branches instead of phased delivery. |\n| A-E002 → A-E004 | Rule 5 | `repo-onboarding` → `konflux-onboarding` always serial; the pipeline needs the repo. |\n| A-E002 → A-E005 | Rule 6 | The operator implementation builds against the onboarded midstream vector store repo/manifests; code needs the repo. |\n| A-E003 → A-E005 | Rule 9 | `license-validation` → general implementation serial; license failures change the dependency set and the approach. |\n| A-E004 ∥ A-E005 (no edge) | Rule 10 | Konflux config is independent of operator code; the build pipeline / image digest coupling is an AC gate (\"pinned productized image digest available\", \"build pipeline green\"), never a DAG edge. |\n| A-E005 → A-E006 | Rules 12/13 | The Platform Operator produces the deployment interface (CR/API) that the Llama Stack integration builds against — build-against artifact, serial. |\n| A-E005 → A-E007 | Rule 13 | The Dashboard integration builds against the operator's CRD surface; serial.