itecture\n40\t  context file — it is a new component. The onboarding chain for the managed\n41\t  posture (Branch A) is assigned to component **Llama Stack** (nearest owning\n42\t  component for a RAG vector store, owned by RHOAI GenAI) pending creation of\n43\t  a canonical component for the vector store. Flag for follow-up.\n44\t- Platform Operator is in the canonical component list but has **no\n45\t  architecture context file** — it is treated as an in-platform component\n46\t  (canonical list membership) but its claims are unvalidated (see Health\n47\t  Warnings).\n48\t\n49\t## Epic List\n50\t\n51\t### Main plan\n52\t\n53\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n54\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n55\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-E001 | Decide the first supported vector store posture (platform-managed vs external-connection-only) | Investigation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n56\t\n57\t### Branch A — outcome: platform-managed (operator-deployed Milvus)\n58\t\n59\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n60\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n61\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E002 | Midstream repo onboarding for the managed vector store (Milvus) | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n62\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E003 | License validation for Milvus and its transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n63\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E004 | Konflux onboarding for the midstream vector store repo | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n64\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E005 | Platform Operator support for deploying the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n65\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E006 | Llama Stack RAG provider integration for the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P1 |\n66\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E007 | Dashboard deploy-and-manage UI for the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n67\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E008 | Documentation for the platform-managed vector store posture | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n68\t\n69\t### Branch B — outcome: external-connection-only\n70\t\n71\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n72\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n73\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E002 | External vector store connection registration with validated connectivity | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n74\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E003 | Llama Stack RAG provider integration for external vector store connections | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P1 |\n75\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E004 | Dashboard connection management UI for external vector stores | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n76\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E005 | Documentation for the external-connection posture | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n77\t\n78\tBranch epic priorities follow priority inheritance from the HLRs they enable\n79\t(an epic blocking all P0 work is P0). Docs epics are P1 via the\n80\tdocs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter priority `Major` →\n81\tP1), not inheritance.\n82\t\n83\t## Dependency DAG\n84\t\n85\tEvery branch epic formally lists the Investigation (RHAISTRAT-9007-E001) in\n86\tits `dependencies` (it is its `gated_by` gate). In the diagram the gate edge\n87\tis drawn to each branch epic; edges within a branch are drawn separately.\n88\t\n89\t```mermaid\n90\tgraph TD\n91\t    E001[\"E001 Investigation: posture decision\"]\n92\t\n93\t    subgraph BranchA[\"Branch A: platform-managed Milvus\"]\n94\t        AE002[\"A-E002 repo-onboarding\"] --> AE004[\"A-E004 konflux-onboarding\"]\n95\t        AE002 --> AE005[\"A-E005 Platform Operator managed deployment\"]\n96\t        AE003[\"A-E003 license-validation\"] --> AE005\n97\t        AE005 --> AE006[\"A-E006 Llama Stack RAG provider\"]\n98\t        AE005 --> AE007[\"A-E007 Dashboard deploy-and-manage UI\"]\n99\t        AE002 --> AE008[\"A-E008 docs\"]\n1