nding the first supported\n46\t  posture, with the evaluation documented and trade-offs made explicit.\n47\t- Confirm the concrete downstream scope implied by the chosen posture (which\n48\t  components change and what each must deliver).\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- A written evaluation exists covering supportability cost,\n53\t  disconnected-environment viability, and time-to-market for both postures.\n54\t- A decision is recorded selecting exactly one posture as the first supported\n55\t  vector store integration, with rationale traceable to the evaluation.\n56\t- The decision record enumerates the downstream work the chosen posture\n57\t  implies (component-level scope), so implementation epics can be confirmed\n58\t  or re-scoped.\n59\t- Stakeholders (product and the affected component teams) have signed off on\n60\t  the decision.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: A decision is reached, with a documented evaluation, on the\n65\t  first supported vector store posture. This epic is the entire fulfillment\n66\t  of HLR-1 and gates all HLR-2 through HLR-5 work.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-831cefdac8eb8373","agent_id":"aa7d072873bbf8959","session_id":"fcd3183f-6a69-447e-9701-c7744c4a517e","uuid":"4641bfbd-177f-4916-94b7-98b2798c8462","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:48:45.056Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a040faa1b321eda3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
