ng team).\n52\t- Reference the productized Milvus image produced by the midstream build\n53\t  pipeline (pinned digest at release time — a configuration reference, not a\n54\t  build-time coupling).\n55\t- Surface deployment status and health in the standard operator status\n56\t  conditions so cluster administrators and the Dashboard can observe it.\n57\t- Include disconnected-environment support consistent with the posture\n58\t  evaluation outcome (no reliance on external image pulls at deploy time).\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- An administrator can deploy the managed vector store through the Platform\n63\t  Operator on a vanilla cluster, and it reaches a healthy running state.\n64\t- The deployment uses the productized image with a pinned digest available\n65\t  from the build pipeline (acceptance gate on the parallel build-pipeline\n66\t  work; not a DAG dependency).\n67\t- The build pipeline for any changed operator code is green (standard\n68\t  pipeline acceptance for operator changes).\n69\t- Upgrade and removal of the managed vector store work without manual cleanup\n70\t  steps.\n71\t- Deployment succeeds in a disconnected environment using mirrored images.\n72\t- The operator deployment model chosen during implementation is validated\n73\t  against the (currently missing) architecture context for the Platform\n74\t  Operator, and any divergence is fed back to the architecture record.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**, managed-path clause: \"administrators can deploy the managed\n79\t  vector store through the Platform Operator with productized images.\"\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-831cefdac8eb8373","agent_id":"aa7d072873bbf8959","session_id":"fcd3183f-6a69-447e-9701-c7744c4a517e","uuid":"48161671-b149-4d25-9e6a-33b868085715","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:48:52.951Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a795fb8ad32be277","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type"