s for the implementing team).\n51\t- Ensure distributions pick up the vector provider automatically when the\n52\t  managed store is deployed in scope, with no hand-edited distribution\n53\t  configs.\n54\t- Verify RAG workflows (embedding storage and retrieval) work end-to-end\n55\t  against the managed store.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A Llama Stack distribution deployed where the managed vector store is\n60\t  available uses it as the RAG/vector provider with no manual config edits.\n61\t- Document-level ingestion and retrieval through the RAG API succeed against\n62\t  the managed store.\n63\t- The integration follows the existing provider-plugin pattern in the\n64\t  Llama Stack distribution (validated against the Llama Stack architecture\n65\t  context).\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: \"Llama Stack distributions can consume the chosen vector\n70\t  store as a RAG provider without hand-editing distribution configs\" —\n71\t  managed-posture fulfillment.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-831cefdac8eb8373","agent_id":"aa7d072873bbf8959","session_id":"fcd3183f-6a69-447e-9701-c7744c4a517e","uuid":"950351db-8d84-465e-ae4d-c7ce51750f9f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:48:54.062Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9af0ca8abb1266d0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
