t (exact config mapping is a design\n51\t  decision for the implementing team).\n52\t- Support the vector store types the posture decision sanctions (the\n53\t  supported-client matrix is fixed by the decision record).\n54\t- Verify RAG workflows (embedding storage and retrieval) work end-to-end\n55\t  against an external store registered via a project connection.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A Llama Stack distribution in a project with a registered, validated\n60\t  external vector store connection uses it as the RAG/vector provider with no\n61\t  manual config edits.\n62\t- Document-level ingestion and retrieval through the RAG API succeed against\n63\t  the external store.\n64\t- Connection failures produce actionable errors surfaced to the user.\n65\t- The integration follows the existing provider-plugin pattern in the Llama\n66\t  Stack distribution (validated against the Llama Stack architecture\n67\t  context).\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: \"Llama Stack distributions can consume the chosen vector\n72\t  store as a RAG provider without hand-editing distribution configs\" —\n73\t  external-posture fulfillment.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-831cefdac8eb8373","agent_id":"aa7d072873bbf8959","session_id":"fcd3183f-6a69-447e-9701-c7744c4a517e","uuid":"577b8b7f-a905-4b2f-958e-55b60ce0b869","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:49:01.094Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-95a24840d94ced23","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
