d — checked against every general implementation in Branch A (A-E005, A-E006,\nA-E007), not just the obvious one — no `konflux-onboarding → general\nimplementation` edge in either direction. The A-E004/A-E005 image-digest\ncoupling is correctly an acceptance criterion (\"pinned productized image digest\navailable\"), not a DAG edge. All 11 branch files set both `branch` (matching\nfilename) and `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-9007-E001`, and no main-plan epic lists a\nbranch epic in its dependencies (E001 has none). Critical path (5 in Branch A,\n4 in Branch B, main plan 1) is within the \"M with new component: 4-5\"\nheuristic. No data/artifact dependency discoverable from epic content is\nmissing from the DAG.\n\n### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\nEach distinct component/team tuple produces a separate epic (Llama Stack/RHOAI\nGenAI, Platform Operator/RHOAI Platform Operator, Dashboard/RHOAI Dashboard,\nDocumentation/RHOAI Documentation). No epic bundles multiple teams. No scope\nduplication within a branch — the A-E006/B-E003 and A-E005/B-E002 pairs are in\nmutually exclusive branches, which the strategy's \"no both postures\" scope\nconstraint requires. Code and content authoring are separated (docs-authoring\nepics are standalone). No epic appears to exceed ~2 weeks. Filing the Milvus\nonboarding chain under Llama Stack is a flagged health warning with a follow-up\nAC (Jira component request), a reasonable treatment given no canonical Milvus\ncomponent exists.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\nE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (posture decision) determines\nwhich entire branch of epics exists — exactly the forking case. All\nImplementation epics produce concrete artifacts. Every branch epic has\n`gated_by` with `gate_failure_impact` carrying both `action: remove` and a\nspecific `fallback_approach` describing the other branch's re-scoping. Every\n`gated_by` target (E001) appears in that epic's direct `dependencies` list.\nE001 itself is un-gated, as appropriate for the root Investigation.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\nType-appropriate signal fields throughout: E001 carries the 5-signal\n`investigation_signals` rubric with `ai_signals: null`; all Implementation\nepics carry the 9-signal `ai_signals` rubric with `investigation_signals:\nnull`. All 12 ai-signals rationale files exist and their values match the\nfrontmatter. Signal values were spot-checked against the actual architecture\ncontext: Llama Stack's context does document the provider-plugin model and\nMilvus/vector providers as an optional dependency (A-E006/B-E003\n`architecture_claims: 1` justified); Dashboard's context documents\nKubernetes-API-only + OdhDashboardConfig feature flags (A-E007/B-E004\n`architecture_claims: 1` justified); Platform Operator has no architecture\ncontext file (A-E005 `architecture_claims: -1` justified — the\ndeploy-a-database assumption is genuinely unvalidated). E001's\n`source_accessibility: 0` correctly reflects that the answer is a pending\nproduct decision, not a lookup. The B-E002 `architecture_claims: 0` (vs\nA-E005's -1) is defensible: the unvalidated assumption is specific to\ndeploying a stateful datastore, not to adding a connection CR.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the HLR text. Rule-mandated ACs are\npresent wherever applicable: both docs-authoring epics have the technical\nreview AC; the konflux-onboarding epic (A-E004) has the pipeline-green AC; the\ncoupled general implementation (A-E005) has both the pinned-digest AC and a\nbuild-pipeline-green AC for operator code; Dashboard epics include\nfeature-flag ACs. No bare draft IDs (e.g. \"E001\") appear in any epic body —\ncross-epic references use full epic IDs or branch-neutral wording.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nAll strategy scope is covered in both branches: managed deployment with\nproductized images and lifecycle (A-E002..A-E005), external registration with\nvalidated connectivity (B-E002), RAG provider consumption, Dashboard surfaces,\nand documentation. The two bounded outcomes of Open Question 1 each have a\ncomplete conditional branch; no third posture is implied by the strategy. The\nevaluation criteria from the open question (supportability cost,\ndisconnected-environment viability, time-to-market) are carried into E001's\nscope and ACs, and disconnected-environment viability is carried further into\nan A-E005 AC. \"Out of scope\" items are honored (branches are mutually\nexclusive; embedding-model lifecycle absent). Strategy gaps (missing\nImpacted Teams / Dependencies / AC / NFR sections) are explicitly surfaced as\nhealth warnings rather than silently dropped.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39653,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-831cefdac8eb8373","agent_id":"aa7d072873bbf8959","session_id":"fcd3183f-6a69-447e-9701-c7744c4a517e","uuid":"be2509a2-7628-470c-b5b7-2fb2fc85381c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:52:33.389Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
