\n39\tand — checked against every general implementation in Branch A (A-E005, A-E006,\n40\tA-E007), not just the obvious one — no `konflux-onboarding → general\n41\timplementation` edge in either direction. The A-E004/A-E005 image-digest\n42\tcoupling is correctly an acceptance criterion (\"pinned productized image digest\n43\tavailable\"), not a DAG edge. All 11 branch files set both `branch` (matching\n44\tfilename) and `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-9007-E001`, and no main-plan epic lists a\n45\tbranch epic in its dependencies (E001 has none). Critical path (5 in Branch A,\n46\t4 in Branch B, main plan 1) is within the \"M with new component: 4-5\"\n47\theuristic. No data/artifact dependency discoverable from epic content is\n48\tmissing from the DAG.\n49\t\n50\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n51\tEach distinct component/team tuple produces a separate epic (Llama Stack/RHOAI\n52\tGenAI, Platform Operator/RHOAI Platform Operator, Dashboard/RHOAI Dashboard,\n53\tDocumentation/RHOAI Documentation). No epic bundles multiple teams. No scope\n54\tduplication within a branch — the A-E006/B-E003 and A-E005/B-E002 pairs are in\n55\tmutually exclusive branches, which the strategy's \"no both postures\" scope\n56\tconstraint requires. Code and content authoring are separated (docs-authoring\n57\tepics are standalone). No epic appears to exceed ~2 weeks. Filing the Milvus\n58\tonboarding chain under Llama Stack is a flagged health warning with a follow-up\n59\tAC (Jira component request), a reasonable treatment given no canonical Milvus\n60\tcomponent exists.\n61\t\n62\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n63\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (posture decision) determines\n64\twhich entire branch of epics exists — exactly the forking case. All\n65\tImplementation epics produce concrete artifacts. Every branch epic has\n66\t`gated_by` with `gate_failure_impact` carrying both `action: remove` and a\n67\tspecific `fallback_approach` describing the other branch's re-scoping. Every\n68\t`gated_by` target (E001) appears in that epic's direct `dependencies` list.\n69\tE001 itself is un-gated, as appropriate for the root Investigation.\n70\t\n71\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n72\tType-appropriate signal fields throughout: E001 carries the 5-signal\n73\t`investigation_signals` rubric with `ai_signals: null`; all Implementation\n74\tepics carry the 9-signal `ai_signals` rubric with `investigation_signals:\n75\tnull`. All 12 ai-signals rationale files exist and their values match the\n76\tfrontmatter. Signal values were spot-checked against the actual architecture\n77\tcontext: Llama Stack's context does document the provider-plugin model and\n78\tMilvus/vector providers as an optional dependency (A-E006/B-E003\n79\t`architecture_claims: 1` justified); Dashboard's context documents\n80\tKubernetes-API-only + OdhDashboardConfig feature flags (A-E007/B-E004\n81\t`architecture_claims: 1` justified); Platform Operator has no architecture\n82\tcontext file (A-E005 `architecture_claims: -1` justified — the\n83\tdeploy-a-database assumption is genuinely unvalidated). E001's\n84\t`source_accessibility: 0` correctly reflects that the answer is a pending\n85\tproduct decision, not a lookup. The B-E002 `architecture_claims: 0` (vs\n86\tA-E005's -1) is defensible: the unvalidated assumption is specific to\n87\tdeploying a stateful datastore, not to adding a connection CR.\n88\t\n89\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n90\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the HLR text. Rule-mandated ACs are\n91\tpresent wherever applicable: both docs-authoring epics have the technical\n92\treview AC; the konflux-onboarding epic (A-E004) has the pipeline-green AC; the\n93\tcoupled general implementation (A-E005) has both the pinned-digest AC and a\n94\tbuild-pipeline-green AC for operator code; Dashboard epics include\n95\tfeature-flag ACs. No bare draft IDs (e.g. \"E001\") appear in any epic body —\n96\tcross-epic references use full epic IDs or branch-neutral wording.\n97\t\n98\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n99\tAll strategy scope is covered in both branches: managed deployment with\n100\tproductized images and lifecycle (A-E002..A-E005), external registration with\n101\tvalidated connectivity (B-E002), RAG provider consumption, Dashboard surfaces,\n102\tand documentation. The two bounded outcomes of Open Question 1 each have a\n103\tcomplete conditional branch; no third posture is implied by the strategy. The\n104\tevaluation criteria from the open question (supportability cost,\n105\tdisconnected-environment viability, time-to-market) are carried into E001's\n106\tscope and ACs, and disconnected-environment viability is carried further into\n107\tan A-E005 AC. \"Out of scope\" items are honored (branches are mutually\n108\texclusive; embedding-model lifecycle absent). Strategy gaps (missing\n109\tImpacted Teams / Dependencies / AC / NFR sections) are explicitly surfaced as\n110\thealth warnings rather than silently dropped.\n111\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adbf797cab941173","agent_id":"aefbfeca159a6d01c","session_id":"fcd3183f-6a69-447e-9701-c7744c4a517e","uuid":"da9b3ed3-1ced-4d6d-a091-2b4b5539e4c9","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:52:58.552Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1b1a098307deb6b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
